    {
      "text": "Compares the WHO-approved respiratory sample types for diagnosing pulmonary TB in children (expectorated sputum, induced sputum, gastric aspirate, nasopharyngeal aspirate, stool) by advantages, disadvantages and caregiver acceptability.",
